===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|markaðr}}, {{m|non|marknaðr||market}}, from northern {{etyl|fro|is}} {{m|fro|markiet}}, from {{etyl|fro|is}} {{m|fro|marchié}}, from {{etyl|la|is}} {{m|la|mercātus||market}}. Cognate with {{etyl|fo|-}} {{m|fo|marknaður}}, Danish and Norwegian ''[[marked]]'', Swedish ''[[marknad]]''.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|markaðar|gen2=markaðs|markaðir}}

# a [[market]]
#: '''''Markaðurinn''' er mettaður.''
#:: The '''market''' is saturated.
# a [[fair]], a [[market]]

